1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Click the + button in a new chat, then turn on Manage Engine.
Your administrator must configure the API connection first.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Check that the Manage Engine badge is visible, then send your question.
Include a person, ticket status and time range, such as open tickets this week.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Review the matching tickets, priorities, statuses and ServiceDesk links.
Check scope warnings: this search scanned only the newest 1,000 tickets.

4
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Ask to create a ticket with a subject, description and requester.
If required information is missing, provide it in your next message.

5
00:00:46,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Review the completed draft, then send its exact Confirm create command.
Use the current draft ID; send Cancel create with that ID to cancel instead.

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
After confirmation, check the creation result and save the ticket ID.
This demonstration created ticket 10510; use the link to open it in ServiceDesk.

7
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Ask: "Show the details of ticket 10510." Use your own ticket ID.
Review its description, requester, assigned technician, priority and status.
